package com.paperlens.app.imaging

// Generated by fitting to a scanner app's results on 17 sample photos (rawScreenshot/Filter: documents,
// signs, a receipt, a screen, packaging, a dark object), pixel-aligned. See [ImageProcessor] for the
// model each [Look] parameterises. Every curve is monotonic, so no page gets tone reversals.

internal class Look(
    /** Paper estimate: max filter radius and box blur (cells), and cells across the short side. */
    val radius: Int,
    val blur: Int,
    val cells: Float,
    /** The paper is never taken darker than this brightness, nor than [relFloor] x its 95th percentile. */
    val floor: Float,
    val relFloor: Float,
    /** How much of the paper's own colour is ignored where it is saturated (coloured areas aren't paper). */
    val neutral: Float,
    /** Thin dark strokes: ratio x (pixel / local brightest)^strokeGamma. */
    val strokeGamma: Float,
    /** Saturation boost on the ratio before the curves. */
    val saturation: Float,
    /** Thin dark strokes deepened after the curves: brightness L below 200 becomes 200 x (L / 200)^deepen. */
    val deepen: Float,
    /** Neutral output from the brightness ratio ([curves] has one entry) instead of per channel. */
    val luma: Boolean,
    /** No Shadow: strongly coloured or dark photos are returned unchanged, as the scanner app does. */
    val skipNonPaper: Boolean,
    /** Ratio (0..RATIO_MAX mapped to 0..255) -> output, per channel R, G, B (or one for [luma]). */
    val curves: List<IntArray>,
)

